## Why this composes (W44-165 vs W44-166)

W44-165 attempted to apply W44-117 EPF seed on photos. EPF seed is
a buttloop-internal recon fix that COMPETES with W44-152's
entropy_mul lift because both adjust the post-recon error signal:
- W44-152 lifts entropy_mul → cost model favors larger blocks →
  fewer high-frequency coefficients → less EPF-correctable signal
- W44-117 EPF seed seeds the buttloop EPF sharpness with a stronger
  starting estimate → buttloop converges to a different recon

The two adjustments to the recon signal can DOUBLE-COMPENSATE
(overshoot the optimum).

W44-166 admits photos to the variant Z TABLE (not seed). Variant Z
is a separate-table-with-different-weights selection at the AC
STRATEGY layer, not the recon layer. It changes which transform
blocks get picked, not the post-recon EPF signal. So variant Z
composes orthogonally with W44-152's outer-table choice — both work
together on different layers of the pipeline.

Crucially, for 1418519 at d=5/6:
- Pre-W44-166: w44_29_lower fires → uses default suppressed table
  (after W44-152 admission). The W44-152 wins are already counted.
- Post-W44-166: SAME admission via W44-152 AND ALSO variant Z is
  swapped in via the new gate. The variant Z table (more aggressive
  dct32x32 lift + dct16x32 lift) selects MORE small-block-friendly
  AC strategies → different strategy distribution → -2.22% bytes
  with mostly-improved SSIM2.

The W44-152 outer-table win is preserved (cost model still uses the
high_d outer table at d∈[3,5]); variant Z is an INNER table swap
that runs on top of the outer table choice.

